.TH THWIP 1 "September 2026" "thwip" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
thwip \- universal coding agent multiplexer for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thwip
.RI [ \-\-project " PATH" ]
.br
.B thwip man
.br
.B thwip install-man
.br
.B thwip \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B thwip
finds the AI coding agents already installed and signed in on this machine
(Codex, Claude Code, and the Antigravity CLI), connects to each through its own
supported protocol, and lets you chat with any of them from one REPL. You can
switch provider or model mid-conversation, keep the text history, and fail over
to another provider when one reports an exhausted usage limit. Direct API keys
for Anthropic, Google, OpenAI, DeepSeek, Groq, OpenRouter, and a local Ollama
server are also supported.
.PP
No credential is copied. Installed CLIs hold their own login, enforce their own
sandbox and approvals, and bill their own plan. Native connections are read-only
by default; Codex asks before operations outside its sandbox.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-project " PATH"
Open the REPL for the given project directory instead of the saved or current one.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B man
Show this manual page.
.TP
.B install-man
Copy this manual page to
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1
so that
.B man thwip
works.
.SH REPL COMMANDS
.TP
.B /switch [agent] [model]
Switch provider (and optionally model). A handoff preview is shown first. Alias:
.BR /sw ", " /s .
.TP
.B /model [id]
Pick a model for the current provider from a numbered list or by ID.
.TP
.B /handoff [agent] [model]
Preview what transfers, what is lost, and the context fit without switching.
.TP
.B /agents ", " /models [agent|tier] ", " /detect
List detected agents, list models (live from the CLI or provider), rescan.
.TP
.B /compact
Ask the current model for a plain-text summary and replace the history with it.
.TP
.B /new ", " /resume [name] ", " /session save|load|list|clear [name]
Start a fresh conversation, resume a saved one, or manage saved sessions.
.TP
.B /diff [staged] ", " /copy ", " /export [path]
Show the project git diff, copy the last response, export the conversation as
Markdown with model attribution.
.TP
.B /limits ", " /usage ", " /cost ", " /status ", " /history
Usage windows reported by each CLI account, API cost estimates, session status,
and the conversation with model badges.
.TP
.B /memory [show|init [area]|edit|update|sync [all]|vault <path>|link]
Project memory: one
.I context.md
per project that every agent reads and helps maintain, filed into your second-brain
vault with cross-project links by stack, area, and tag. Updates proposed by the model
are shown as a diff and written only after confirmation.
.TP
.B /key [provider]
Enter a direct API key with hidden input.
.TP
.B /native codex
Save the session and replace thwip with the Codex CLI itself.
.TP
.B !command
Run a shell command in the project without involving a model.
.TP
.B @path
Attach a project file's content to your message.
.TP
.B /help ", " /about ", " /quit
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Open the switcher.
.TP
.B Ctrl+T
Show status.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Interrupt the current response, command, or prompt. At the main prompt, exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B THWIP_CONFIG_DIR
Configuration directory (default
.IR ~/.thwip ).
.TP
.B THWIP_OPENAI_BASE_URL ", " THWIP_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL ", " THWIP_GOOGLE_BASE_URL ", " THWIP_DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL ", " THWIP_GROQ_BASE_URL ", " THWIP_OPENROUTER_BASE_URL
Point a direct adapter at a proxy, gateway, or OpenAI-compatible server.
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ", " GEMINI_API_KEY ", " OPENAI_API_KEY ", " DEEPSEEK_API_KEY ", " GROQ_API_KEY ", " OPENROUTER_API_KEY
Direct API keys. A key takes precedence over the native CLI connection for that provider.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.thwip/config.toml
Defaults, keys entered with /key, endpoint overrides, fallback chain, display settings,
and the [memory] section (file name, vault path, quit-time offer).
.TP
.I <project>/context.md
The project's memory file, shared by every agent used in that project.
.TP
.I ~/.thwip/sessions/
Saved sessions, including the native CLI session IDs used to resume each provider.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR codex (1),
.BR claude (1),
.BR agy (1)
